            <encodings>
              <color column='[federated.0ynqkqv1tw4y881djxjy10809cts].[none:Calculation_639511184137678854:nk]' />
            </encodings>
            <customized-tooltip>
              <formatted-text>
                <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000'>Calibrated:</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='8'>based on 40-20-40 logic &amp; calibrated by incrementality tests (applies to Display Channels only)</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000'>Rules for Calibration:</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='8'>Country factors overrule segment factors, segment factors overrule global factors</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='8'>Country Factor: 2 significant tests showing similar results</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='8'>Segment Factor: 3 significant results</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='8'>Global Factor: 5 significant tests in min. 2 segments</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='8'>In order to build segment &amp; country factors, we use a consistent methodology by removing outliers, applying the average - “top/bottom” methodology. </run>
                <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='8' italic='true'>&quot;</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000'>40-20-40:</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='8'>- based on digital touchpoints of the user</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='8'>- gives 40% of the order to the first and last touchpoints; 20% goes to all all touchpoints in between (distributed equally)</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='8'>- can be broken down by all dimensions</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000'>Limitations on iOS Fix:</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='8'>- The acquisitions data with the fix </run>
                <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='8'>won&apos;t</run>
                <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='8'> be available</run>
                <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='8'> before 2021</run>
                <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='8'>.</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='8'>- The acquisitions data with the fix </run>
                <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='8'>won&apos;t</run>
                <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='8'> be available on a </run>
                <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='8'>daily</run>
                <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='8'> level.</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='8'>- The filters on channels, entities and platform type should work as expected.</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='8'>- The fix won&apos;t be applied to the orders. </run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='8'>- The SEM re-acquisitions through smart banner are not a part of the iOS fix. </run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='8'>- For further information please click on the blue point or `Attribution Model INFO ` text.</run>
              </formatted-text>
            </customized-tooltip>
            <style>
